Fill Disposition and Note on the 17 rows that escalated to ops/conductor-log.md as
AUDIT_FINDING_UNTRIAGED on 2026-09-04 and 2026-09-05. Append-only: 17 rows changed in place,
no row added or removed, line count unchanged (128). Ledger parses clean: 0 malformed,
OPEN 113 -> 96.

Every finding was verified against the source or the artifact, not the audit report. The
reports were recovered from git (f32c34228a, 601c8fe7a5, e62a74538a, 9ee9323ece) because the
conductor overwrites them at each milestone-close. The live helpers were run on every artifact
the reports named, and the full gate was run on scratchpad COPIES of the four escalated
artifacts. results/** was read, never written.

Dispositions:
- FIXED (1): worktree_import_guard.py, already closed by 5d3f03326c (tree-wide conftest).
- WONTFIX (2): _moat_rigor_headroom_state (named input is an informative null with 0.34
  headroom, not a miss) and _moat_rigor_claims_null (normalisation at line 7206 unwraps the
  field before this helper's only caller runs; verified on exp5007).
- ACCEPTED (14): the other nine adversarial_verify.py rows, capstone_milestone_rot_lint.py,
  and the four claim-class artifacts (exp6275, exp6960, exp6961, exp6976).

Shared root for nine of the eleven adversarial_verify.py rows: the moat-rigor family recognises
a claim only through fixed marker lists written in one track's spelling. The corpus states the
same concept as `moat_survives` (3 artifacts), `beats_vote` (19 verdicts, 25 delta fields;
majority vote IS self-consistency), a `status` field, a nested `verifier_over_sc_lift.delta`,
and a qualified `MET_*` status. One widening closes all nine; no redesign.

Two side findings recorded in the notes, not fixed here: experiment_6847 trips the capstone
lint's existing rule on the default glob (landed via a hook-skipping conductor commit), and
experiment_5008, the artifact that shipped the moat-rigor check, is flagged_adversarial by that
check's own `success_moat` marker.

